window.SCHOOL_LISTENING={"../assets/media/3663f172862b4da610b9c85be278e9f80ee5725051d9f7dfc5c4f887c8b63065.mp3":[{"id":"PPT_3663f172862b4da6","audioId":"PPT_3663f172862b4da6","title":"Book 3 · Unit 6 · RW · READING 2","subtitle":"READING 2 · source slide 112","duration":266.53,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.12,"text":"Deep fakes,","coverage":1},{"start":1.6,"end":3.08,"text":"benefit or threat.","coverage":1},{"start":4.1,"end":7.6,"text":"You have probably already seen something like this online.","coverage":1},{"start":8.2,"end":12.62,"text":"The head of one actor on the body of a completely different actor.","coverage":1},{"start":13.46,"end":16.56,"text":"This type of image is created by a computer,","coverage":1},{"start":17.12,"end":19.1,"text":"and it is called a deep fake.","coverage":1},{"start":20.22,"end":30,"text":"Deep fakes use a form of artificial intelligence in which a computer model is trained to use information in the same way as the human brain.","coverage":1},{"start":30.7,"end":37.54,"text":"It can create images and voices that look and sound almost like real people,","coverage":1},{"start":38.22,"end":39.2,"text":"including actors,","coverage":1},{"start":39.74,"end":40.26,"text":"politicians,","coverage":1},{"start":40.74,"end":42.36,"text":"and other famous people.","coverage":1},{"start":42.94,"end":44.08,"text":"In the past,","coverage":1},{"start":44.4,"end":50.86,"text":"only experts were able to use this technology, but now anyone can create a deep fake.","coverage":1},{"start":50.86,"end":55.14,"text":"This is causing both excitement and worry.","coverage":1},{"start":56.78,"end":60.32,"text":"The most familiar use of deep fakes is in entertainment.","coverage":1},{"start":61.18,"end":61.94,"text":"For example,","coverage":1},{"start":62.34,"end":66.76,"text":"deep fake technology can make actors in films look much younger.","coverage":1},{"start":67.72,"end":69.68,"text":"It works much better than makeup.","coverage":1},{"start":71,"end":77.16,"text":"Directors can also use it to produce the image or voice of actors who are not available.","coverage":1},{"start":77.16,"end":83.56,"text":"For example, a director may discover a mistake and want to film a scene again,","coverage":1},{"start":84.1,"end":87.36,"text":"but the actors are already working on other projects.","coverage":1},{"start":88.12,"end":93.58,"text":"The scene can be recreated by artificial intelligence without the live actors.","coverage":1},{"start":94.46,"end":94.88,"text":"How?","coverage":1},{"start":95.84,"end":101.52,"text":"Deep fake technology uses the rest of the film to learn the actor's appearance,","coverage":1},{"start":101.84,"end":103.14,"text":"speech, and movement.","coverage":1},{"start":103.14,"end":107.14,"text":"It can even recreate actors who are dead.","coverage":1},{"start":108.52,"end":108.98,"text":"Clearly,","coverage":1},{"start":109.32,"end":112.45,"text":"this technology offers the film industry many benefits.","coverage":1},{"start":113.44,"end":113.94,"text":"However,","coverage":1},{"start":114.44,"end":117.2,"text":"this technology also creates problems.","coverage":1},{"start":118.1,"end":118.62,"text":"Today,","coverage":1},{"start":118.94,"end":121.06,"text":"so much of our lives are online.","coverage":1},{"start":122.02,"end":125.16,"text":"What if someone creates a deep fake of you?","coverage":1},{"start":125.86,"end":129.08,"text":"Could it be used to get access to your bank account,","coverage":1},{"start":129.76,"end":130.84,"text":"your health records?","coverage":1},{"start":130.84,"end":132.98,"text":"In 2020,","coverage":1},{"start":133.52,"end":138.94,"text":"thieves created a deep fake voice of a bank manager in the United Arab Emirates.","coverage":1},{"start":139.58,"end":143.12,"text":"They used it to steal $35 million.","coverage":1},{"start":143.98,"end":146.36,"text":"As the technology improves,","coverage":1},{"start":146.96,"end":150.4,"text":"these threats to security will definitely increase.","coverage":1},{"start":152,"end":154.58,"text":"Deep fakes can also threaten privacy.","coverage":1},{"start":154.58,"end":157.26,"text":"Our personal information,","coverage":1},{"start":157.58,"end":158.6,"text":"including photos,","coverage":1},{"start":159.12,"end":161.16,"text":"is often available on the internet.","coverage":1},{"start":162.24,"end":166.5,"text":"Someone could use your photo and put it on someone else's body.","coverage":1},{"start":167.42,"end":171.8,"text":"Some celebrities have already found their own images on the internet.","coverage":1},{"start":172.88,"end":178.3,"text":"They are doing things they never did and saying things they never said.","coverage":1},{"start":179.14,"end":182.22,"text":"This can be embarrassing or even dangerous.","coverage":1},{"start":182.22,"end":188.24,"text":"It is very difficult to control these images once they appear on the internet.","coverage":1},{"start":189.48,"end":190.08,"text":"Finally,","coverage":1},{"start":190.62,"end":194.18,"text":"deep fakes can be used to spread false information.","coverage":1},{"start":195.04,"end":198.98,"text":"Today, when we watch the news on television or online,","coverage":1},{"start":199.44,"end":202.1,"text":"we generally believe everything is real.","coverage":1},{"start":202.8,"end":209.1,"text":"We believe that the heads, bodies, and voices all belong to the same real people.","coverage":1},{"start":209.1,"end":212.36,"text":"As deep fake technology improves,","coverage":1},{"start":213.24,"end":215.04,"text":"that will probably change.","coverage":1},{"start":215.7,"end":220.96,"text":"We will not be able to trust what we see and hear because it could be fake.","coverage":1},{"start":221.92,"end":224.34,"text":"Deep fakes can change today's news,","coverage":1},{"start":225.02,"end":227.22,"text":"but they may also change history.","coverage":1},{"start":228.22,"end":229.14,"text":"For example,","coverage":1},{"start":229.46,"end":235.94,"text":"someone could discover a lost video of a famous person saying terrible things.","coverage":1},{"start":235.94,"end":241.44,"text":"Deep fakes may change how we view our world and our past.","coverage":1},{"start":243.1,"end":248.16,"text":"Although this technology offers important benefits to the entertainment industry,","coverage":1},{"start":248.78,"end":251.98,"text":"it also presents some frightening possibilities.","coverage":1},{"start":253.02,"end":255.96,"text":"Experts advise that we should use the same tool,","coverage":1},{"start":256.28,"end":257.58,"text":"artificial intelligence,","coverage":1},{"start":257.98,"end":264.61,"text":"to tackle these problems and make sure that this technology is used responsibly.","coverage":1}],"file":"6fe5654ce5f5ba6c543c.js","track":0,"media":"../assets/media/3663f172862b4da610b9c85be278e9f80ee5725051d9f7dfc5c4f887c8b63065.mp3"}],"../assets/media/3bd46e4cfc5b3992c41c0d5c030c4f9dbcd8a71b095b61a30881d7bd6bd0cea1.mp3":[{"id":"PPT_3bd46e4cfc5b3992","audioId":"PPT_3bd46e4cfc5b3992","title":"Book 3 · Unit 6 · RW · READING 1","subtitle":"READING 1 · source slide 36","duration":249.52,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.3,"text":"The magic of mimicry.","coverage":1},{"start":3.6,"end":8.18,"text":"To mimic people means to copy their speech, dress, or behavior.","coverage":1},{"start":8.88,"end":9.8,"text":"In contrast,","coverage":1},{"start":10.2,"end":11.08,"text":"in science,","coverage":1},{"start":11.44,"end":21.1,"text":"mimic means copying ideas from nature or natural processes to prevent or solve problems or to create helpful products.","coverage":1},{"start":21.94,"end":28.34,"text":"The influence of this so -called biomimicry can be seen in a huge range of everyday products,","coverage":1},{"start":28.76,"end":30.4,"text":"from clothing to cars.","coverage":1},{"start":31.84,"end":35.94,"text":"Perhaps the best known example of biomimicry is Velcro.","coverage":1},{"start":36.7,"end":42.24,"text":"It was invented in 1941 by a Swiss engineer called George de Mestral.","coverage":1},{"start":43.1,"end":43.78,"text":"One day,","coverage":1},{"start":44.12,"end":48.22,"text":"Mestral noticed the burdock seeds that stuck to his dog's hair.","coverage":1},{"start":49,"end":50.18,"text":"Under the microscope,","coverage":1},{"start":50.58,"end":57.28,"text":"he discovered that these seeds had hooks on them, so they stuck to loops on clothing or hair.","coverage":1},{"start":58.22,"end":62.6,"text":"Mestral copied this idea and created two strips of material,","coverage":1},{"start":63.18,"end":67,"text":"one with tiny hooks and the other with loose loops.","coverage":1},{"start":67.78,"end":69.66,"text":"When he put both strips together,","coverage":1},{"start":70.08,"end":71.42,"text":"they stuck like glue.","coverage":1},{"start":72.22,"end":72.66,"text":"However,","coverage":1},{"start":73.14,"end":74.28,"text":"unlike with glue,","coverage":1},{"start":74.7,"end":78.24,"text":"he could peel the strips apart and reattach them.","coverage":1},{"start":79.28,"end":88.26,"text":"Velcro was initially unpopular with fashion companies, but after it was used by NASA to stop items from floating in space,","coverage":1},{"start":88.72,"end":91.92,"text":"it became popular with children's clothing companies.","coverage":1},{"start":92.82,"end":97.64,"text":"Today, it is used to fasten everything from lunch bags to shoes.","coverage":1},{"start":99.34,"end":101.76,"text":"Another example comes from the ocean,","coverage":1},{"start":102.14,"end":108.16,"text":"where mussels can stick to surfaces even when the water is moving very fast around them.","coverage":1},{"start":108.88,"end":114.22,"text":"Mussels produce a very strong adhesive that works in wet conditions.","coverage":1},{"start":115.18,"end":123.96,"text":"Scientists were able to copy this material and found that it was three times stronger than other underwater adhesives.","coverage":1},{"start":124.74,"end":128.4,"text":"Another advantage is that it will not hurt the environment.","coverage":1},{"start":129.82,"end":130.54,"text":"For NASA,","coverage":1},{"start":130.96,"end":132.18,"text":"protecting astronauts'","coverage":1},{"start":132.64,"end":135.34,"text":"eyes from the sun's rays is very important,","coverage":1},{"start":135.73,"end":140.82,"text":"but protecting their eyes from other dangerous radiation is also essential.","coverage":1},{"start":141.86,"end":147.32,"text":"Scientists studied how eagles and falcons clearly recognize their prey.","coverage":1},{"start":148.04,"end":152.86,"text":"Scientists discovered that the birds have yellow oil in their eyes,","coverage":1},{"start":153.38,"end":158.38,"text":"which filters out harmful radiation and allows them to see very clearly.","coverage":1},{"start":159.1,"end":160.94,"text":"NASA copied this oil,","coverage":1},{"start":161.5,"end":166.28,"text":"and it is now used by astronauts and pilots in eagle -eyes glasses.","coverage":1},{"start":167.36,"end":170.34,"text":"In addition to protecting eyes from dangerous rays,","coverage":1},{"start":170.88,"end":175.24,"text":"these sunglasses also improve vision in different weather conditions,","coverage":1},{"start":175.86,"end":176.74,"text":"such as fog,","coverage":1},{"start":177.3,"end":177.64,"text":"sunlight,","coverage":1},{"start":178.16,"end":179.86,"text":"or just normal light.","coverage":1},{"start":181.24,"end":182.06,"text":"For birds,","coverage":1},{"start":182.62,"end":186.02,"text":"cities full of tall glass buildings are a problem.","coverage":1},{"start":187.02,"end":189.68,"text":"Spider's webs may be the solution.","coverage":1},{"start":190.58,"end":192.58,"text":"Birds cannot see the glass,","coverage":1},{"start":193,"end":198,"text":"so more than a billion of them fly into buildings and die every year.","coverage":1},{"start":198.68,"end":199.22,"text":"However,","coverage":1},{"start":199.66,"end":201.72,"text":"they can see spider's webs,","coverage":1},{"start":202.06,"end":203.76,"text":"and they try to avoid them.","coverage":1},{"start":204.54,"end":205,"text":"So,","coverage":1},{"start":205.4,"end":210.02,"text":"engineers have used this idea in the invention of a new kind of window.","coverage":1},{"start":210.88,"end":215.64,"text":"These windows have tiny lines on them that look like spider's webs,","coverage":1},{"start":216.44,"end":222.5,"text":"birds can see them, but the lines are so thin that humans cannot see them easily.","coverage":1},{"start":223.26,"end":228.7,"text":"It is likely that we will see these bird -friendly windows on more buildings in the future,","coverage":1},{"start":229.18,"end":230.26,"text":"and as a result,","coverage":1},{"start":230.64,"end":233.14,"text":"a significant drop in bird deaths.","coverage":1},{"start":234.6,"end":236.48,"text":"As these examples illustrate,","coverage":1},{"start":237.18,"end":241.18,"text":"biomimicry appears to have an unlimited number of applications.","coverage":1},{"start":241.18,"end":247.54,"text":"It will be interesting to see which problems nature helps us solve in the future.","coverage":1}],"file":"ed4136eba0e349885021.js","track":0,"media":"../assets/media/3bd46e4cfc5b3992c41c0d5c030c4f9dbcd8a71b095b61a30881d7bd6bd0cea1.mp3"}]};
window.SCHOOL_SOURCE_ANSWERS=[{"text":"1 Where does most energy come from in your country? Possible sources include gas, oil, coal, wind and sunlight.","slide":4,"shape":"18","bookPage":"126"},{"text":"2 What do people in your country think about the use of fossil fuels? Some people worry about the effects of fossil fuels on the climate.","slide":4,"shape":"20","bookPage":"126"},{"text":"3 Is the government working to find other forms of energy? A possible example is investment in wind or solar energy.","slide":4,"shape":"6","bookPage":"126"},{"text":"1 How do you think the first photo is related to energy? The sun is an important source of energy.","slide":6,"shape":"29","bookPage":"126"},{"text":"2 Look at the second photo. What are some dangers of this kind of energy? An accident can release harmful radioactive material.","slide":6,"shape":"30","bookPage":"126"},{"text":"3 Where do you think we will get most of our energy in the future? We may use more renewable sources, such as wind and sunlight.","slide":6,"shape":"31","bookPage":"126"},{"text":"1  A factory producing electricity is a power station.","slide":14,"shape":"7","bookPage":"126"},{"text":"2  An important discovery is a breakthrough.","slide":14,"shape":"8","bookPage":"126"},{"text":"3  To make something happen again is to recreate it.","slide":14,"shape":"9","bookPage":"126"},{"text":"4  A chemical change is a reaction.","slide":14,"shape":"10","bookPage":"126"},{"text":"5  Force applied against something is pressure.","slide":14,"shape":"11","bookPage":"126"},{"text":"6  An amount without a limit is unlimited.","slide":14,"shape":"12","bookPage":"126"},{"text":"2 Fusion technology offers the best and safest possibility of getting unlimited clean energy, but it is still too expensive.","slide":17,"shape":"13","bookPage":"127"},{"text":"1 Fusion is much safer than nuclear fission.","slide":20,"shape":"15","bookPage":"127"},{"text":"2 Fusion needs extreme heat or pressure or both.","slide":20,"shape":"17","bookPage":"127"},{"text":"3 Fusion uses hydrogen molecules from sea water.","slide":21,"shape":"15","bookPage":"127"},{"text":"4 Fusion is clean. It creates zero carbon.","slide":21,"shape":"17","bookPage":"127"},{"text":"1 Which do you think is more important: saving energy or finding new sources of energy? Explain your answer. I think saving energy matters now while researchers develop new sources.","slide":23,"shape":"16","bookPage":"127"},{"text":"2 Do you think we will have fusion energy in your lifetime? Why / Why not? It could become available, but the video says cost and efficiency remain problems.","slide":23,"shape":"18","bookPage":"127"},{"text":"5  The human brain has an almost unlimited memory capacity, far more than that of a\ncomputer.","slide":34,"shape":"6","bookPage":"128"},{"text":"6  If you want to be an engineer or a scientist, it’s essential that you have good\nqualifications in Science and Maths.","slide":34,"shape":"7","bookPage":"128"},{"text":"7  The engineer used diagrams to illustrate his point about the mechanics of suspension\nbridges like the Golden Gate Bridge.","slide":34,"shape":"8","bookPage":"128"},{"text":"1 Bio- is a prefix which means ‘life’. What words do you know that start with bio-? Biology, biography, biomedicine and biometrics.","slide":46,"shape":"19","bookPage":"128"},{"text":"2 What do you think mimicry and biomimicry mean? Mimicry means copying; biomimicry means copying from nature.","slide":46,"shape":"21","bookPage":"128"},{"text":"3 Can you think of any inventions which copy their shape or function from something in nature? Some buildings copy the structure of beehives.","slide":46,"shape":"6","bookPage":"128"},{"text":"An adhesive is a material that can make things stick together.","slide":49,"shape":"7","bookPage":"129"},{"text":"c Many useful products have been designed using biomimicry.","slide":61,"shape":"13","bookPage":"130"},{"text":"Velcro copies burdock seeds.","slide":63,"shape":"15","bookPage":"130"},{"text":"The underwater adhesive copies mussels.","slide":63,"shape":"17","bookPage":"130"},{"text":"Eagle Eyes glasses copy eagles and falcons.","slide":64,"shape":"15","bookPage":"130"},{"text":"Bird-friendly windows copy spider’s webs.","slide":64,"shape":"17","bookPage":"130"},{"text":"1 Which two features of Velcro make the strips stick together? Tiny hooks and loose loops.","slide":77,"shape":"15","bookPage":"130"},{"text":"2 What are some uses of Velcro? Children’s clothing, lunch bags and shoes; NASA also used it to stop items floating in space.","slide":77,"shape":"17","bookPage":"130"},{"text":"3 What product can be used underwater? The adhesive copied from mussels.","slide":77,"shape":"6","bookPage":"130"},{"text":"4 What does adhesive allow the mussels to do? It lets them stick to rocks or other surfaces.","slide":78,"shape":"15","bookPage":"130"},{"text":"5 Whose eyes did NASA want to protect from dangerous radiation? Astronauts’ eyes.","slide":78,"shape":"17","bookPage":"130"},{"text":"6 What special feature of an eagle’s eyes was copied to make sunglasses? The yellow oil that filters out harmful radiation.","slide":78,"shape":"6","bookPage":"130"},{"text":"7 What feature of the new kind of window saves birds’ lives? Tiny lines that look like spider’s webs.","slide":79,"shape":"19","bookPage":"130"},{"text":"1 Why do you think Velcro became popular with children’s clothing companies? Velcro can make it easier for children to fasten clothes themselves.","slide":91,"shape":"19","bookPage":"131"},{"text":"2 What uses do you think the adhesive from mussels have? It might be useful for equipment in the ocean.","slide":91,"shape":"21","bookPage":"131"},{"text":"3 Do you think a lot of new buildings will have bird-friendly windows in the future? They could become common if they are effective and affordable.","slide":91,"shape":"6","bookPage":"131"},{"text":"11. Paragraph A\nAnswer: iv","slide":94,"shape":"5","bookPage":null},{"text":"12. Paragraph B\nAnswer: vi","slide":95,"shape":"5","bookPage":null},{"text":"1 It is important to protect your personal data, such as your financial and health information. b belonging to a specific person","slide":109,"shape":"14","bookPage":"132"},{"text":"2 Actors use their voices and the movement of their bodies to express emotion. a change of position","slide":109,"shape":"16","bookPage":"132"},{"text":"3 The internet helps to spread information and ideas around the world. b tell a lot of people about something","slide":109,"shape":"6","bookPage":"132"},{"text":"4 Actors often change their appearance so that their fans cannot recognize them. b how someone looks","slide":110,"shape":"14","bookPage":"132"},{"text":"5 This building does not have good security. The doors are unlocked and the windows are open. a protection against threats","slide":110,"shape":"16","bookPage":"132"},{"text":"6 Actors often lose their privacy after they become famous. People want to know all about their lives. a the right to keep your life secret","slide":110,"shape":"6","bookPage":"132"},{"text":"7 Experts say images are more powerful than words. They are easier to understand and remember. b pictures","slide":111,"shape":"18","bookPage":"132"},{"text":"1 Do you believe everything you read on the internet? How do you determine what is true and what is not? I compare sources and check who published the information and what evidence they provide.","slide":113,"shape":"15","bookPage":"132"},{"text":"2 When you see pictures of people on the internet, can you trust that they are real? What about images of famous people? Images may be edited, so I check their source and context.","slide":113,"shape":"17","bookPage":"132"},{"text":"The author’s overall view is more negative. One body paragraph develops entertainment benefits; three develop threats to security, privacy and trustworthy information. The conclusion stresses frightening possibilities and responsible use.","slide":126,"shape":"13","bookPage":"134"},{"text":"Benefits of deepfake technology\nfor entertainment industry\nProblems that deepfake\ntechnology creates\nMake actors look younger\nThreats to security\nRecreate scenes without live actors\nThreats to privacy\nRecreate actors who have died\nSpreading false information","slide":140,"shape":"12","bookPage":"134"},{"text":"1 Privacy: Some celebrities have already found their own images on the internet. They are doing things they never did and saying things they never said!","slide":149,"shape":"20","bookPage":"134"},{"text":"2 Security: In 2020, thieves created a deepfake voice of a bank manager in the United Arab Emirates. They used it to steal $35 million!","slide":149,"shape":"22","bookPage":"134"},{"text":"3 Misinformation: For example, someone could ‘discover’ a ‘lost’ video of a famous person saying terrible things.","slide":149,"shape":"6","bookPage":"134"},{"text":"1 Deepfake technology uses the rest of the film to ‘learn’ the actors’ appearance, speech and movement. The computer processes patterns in data; it does not learn in exactly the way a person does.","slide":160,"shape":"17","bookPage":"134"},{"text":"2 For example, someone could ‘discover’ a ‘lost’ video of a famous person saying terrible things. The video may have been fabricated rather than genuinely lost and discovered.","slide":160,"shape":"19","bookPage":"134"},{"text":"1  In years to come, biofuels will definitely become more important. (100%)","slide":165,"shape":"6","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"2  Genetic modification probably won’t be very controversial before the end of the decade.\n(20%)","slide":165,"shape":"7","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"3  In the near future, electronic human implants could possibly become very common. (50%)","slide":165,"shape":"8","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"4  Biomimicry will probably be a growing industry before too long. (90%)","slide":165,"shape":"9","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"5  Self-driving cars will definitely be everyday products within the next ten years. (100%)","slide":165,"shape":"10","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"6  People definitely won’t be living on Mars within the next few years. (0%)","slide":165,"shape":"11","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"1 In years to come, biofuels will definitely become more important.","slide":167,"shape":"18","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"2 Genetic modification probably won’t be very controversial before the end of the decade.","slide":167,"shape":"20","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"3 In the near future, electronic human implants could possibly become very common.","slide":167,"shape":"6","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"4 Biomimicry will probably be a growing industry before too long.","slide":167,"shape":"8","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"5 Self-driving cars will definitely be everyday products within the next ten years.","slide":168,"shape":"18","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"6 People definitely won’t be living on Mars within the next few years.","slide":168,"shape":"20","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"1 Robots will probably help with more household tasks.","slide":170,"shape":"18","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"2 We could possibly see new forms of public transport.","slide":170,"shape":"20","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"3 People probably won’t stop using all paper books.","slide":170,"shape":"6","bookPage":"135"},{"text":"de-: decrease, deactivate, defrost","slide":181,"shape":"15","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"dis-: disagree, disengage, disobey","slide":181,"shape":"17","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"en-: enable, enact, enclose","slide":181,"shape":"6","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"pre-: preview, prepare, predict","slide":181,"shape":"8","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"re-: rebuild, reread, rewrite","slide":182,"shape":"15","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"trans-: transport, transfer, translate","slide":182,"shape":"17","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"un-, in-, im-: unlikely, uncertain, impossible","slide":182,"shape":"6","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"Prefix\nMeaning\nExample\nde-\nbecome less, go down\ndecrease, deactivate, defrost\ndis-\nopposite\ndisagree, disengage, disobey\nen-\ncause\nenable, enact, enclose\npre-\nbefore\npreview, prepare, predict","slide":183,"shape":"13","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"Prefix\nMeaning\nExample\nre-\nagain\nrebuild, reread, rewrite\ntrans-\nacross, through\ntransport, transfer, translate\nun-, in-, im-\nreverse, not\nunlikely, uncertain, impossible","slide":184,"shape":"13","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"5  This laboratory is very disorganized.\nThis laboratory is neat.  O","slide":189,"shape":"6","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"6  The font on your presentation is too small. Can you enlarge it?\nCan you make it bigger?  S","slide":189,"shape":"7","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"1 We will probably rethink how we use energy.","slide":191,"shape":"15","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"2 New software could possibly translate more languages.","slide":191,"shape":"17","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"3 Some devices will probably decrease in size.","slide":191,"shape":"6","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"4 Designers could possibly enlarge screens without making devices heavier.","slide":191,"shape":"8","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"5 Some unsafe technologies probably won’t remain popular.","slide":192,"shape":"19","bookPage":"136"},{"text":"A library app could show available books. Students may spend less time searching. They could check a title before visiting.","slide":196,"shape":"6","bookPage":null},{"text":"A very high shelf is unlikely to suit every classroom user. Some students may not reach it. A lower shelf could be a better alternative.","slide":196,"shape":"9","bookPage":null},{"text":"11. The finished fastening differs from the natural seed in both size and material.\nAnswer: F","slide":202,"shape":"5","bookPage":null},{"text":"12. The designers clearly state a limit on their final claim.\nAnswer: F","slide":202,"shape":"8","bookPage":null},{"text":"12. Paragraph B\nAnswer: v","slide":206,"shape":"5","bookPage":null},{"text":"A lamp with a large switch may help someone working in low light. The switch would be easier to find. However, the lamp might take up more desk space. Users could test it in a small study area.","slide":211,"shape":"6","bookPage":null},{"text":"The app could add a simple picture map. New users might find places more easily. However, the map may need frequent updates. The team could first test it in one small building.","slide":211,"shape":"9","bookPage":null},{"text":"medicine: CT scanner, insulin pump, 3-D imaging","slide":216,"shape":"15","bookPage":"137"},{"text":"home: solar roof; low-flush toilet","slide":216,"shape":"17","bookPage":"137"},{"text":"space: Mars rover; International Space Station","slide":216,"shape":"6","bookPage":"137"},{"text":"transport: e-bikes; driverless cars","slide":216,"shape":"8","bookPage":"137"},{"text":"entertainment: HD TV; 3-D glasses","slide":217,"shape":"15","bookPage":"137"},{"text":"computers: tablet computers; cloud computing","slide":217,"shape":"17","bookPage":"137"},{"text":"agriculture: hydroponics","slide":217,"shape":"6","bookPage":"137"},{"text":"Areas of technology\nInventions\nmedicine\nCT scanner, insulin pump, 3-D imaging\nhome\nsolar roof; low-flush toilet\nspace\nMars rover; International Space Station\ntransport\ne-bikes; driverless cars\nentertainment\nHD TV; 3-D glasses\ncomputers\ntablet computers; cloud computing\nagriculture\nhydroponics","slide":218,"shape":"12","bookPage":"137"},{"text":"Invention 1: driverless cars. Possible advantages: comfortable journeys; less need to control the car yourself. Possible disadvantages: cost; dependence on complex technology.","slide":223,"shape":"15","bookPage":"138"},{"text":"Invention 2: tablet computers. Advantages: portable; many applications. Disadvantages: can be expensive; less convenient than a large screen for some tasks.","slide":223,"shape":"17","bookPage":"138"},{"text":"Advantages\nDisadvantages\ncomfortable journeys; less need to control the car yourself\ncost; dependence on complex technology","slide":224,"shape":"13","bookPage":"138"},{"text":"Advantages\nDisadvantages\nportable; many applications\ncan be expensive; less convenient than a large screen for some tasks","slide":225,"shape":"13","bookPage":"138"},{"text":"Driverless cars: They could remain useful if their practical limitations are addressed.","slide":229,"shape":"15","bookPage":"138"},{"text":"Tablet computers: They will probably remain useful for people who want a portable device larger than a phone.","slide":229,"shape":"17","bookPage":"138"},{"text":"1 Scientists have developed robots that are able to do dangerous work. Which robots?","slide":233,"shape":"14","bookPage":"139"},{"text":"2 A journalist wrote about a video that had been ‘lost.’ Which video?","slide":233,"shape":"16","bookPage":"139"},{"text":"3 Inventions that are based on nature have many advantages. Which inventions?","slide":233,"shape":"6","bookPage":"139"},{"text":"4 Deepfake technology can recreate images of actors who are not available. Which actors?","slide":233,"shape":"8","bookPage":"139"},{"text":"5 The images that are created by deepfake technology can seem very real. Which images?","slide":234,"shape":"18","bookPage":"139"},{"text":"1 There are many news stories about celebrities. Celebrities are the victims of deepfake technology.There are many news stories about celebrities who are the victims of deepfake technology.","slide":236,"shape":"17","bookPage":"139"},{"text":"2 There is a huge amount of new investment in biofuels. Biofuels are cleaner and more sustainable than fossil fuels.There is a huge amount of new investment in biofuels that are cleaner and more sustainable than fossil fuels.","slide":236,"shape":"19","bookPage":"139"},{"text":"3 Scientists at Cambridge University have published research in biomimicry. The research will have a major influence in the field.Scientists at Cambridge University have published research in biomimicry that will have a major influence in the field.","slide":237,"shape":"18","bookPage":"139"},{"text":"Adnan is the student who sits in the front row.","slide":239,"shape":"13","bookPage":"140"},{"text":"1 Deepfakes are based on deep learning, which is a form of artificial intelligence.","slide":242,"shape":"14","bookPage":"140"},{"text":"2 The adhesive produced by the mussels, which scientists have been studying for years, is now used in industry and medicine.","slide":242,"shape":"16","bookPage":"140"},{"text":"3 Another example of biomimicry is a new kind of window, which is based on a spider’s web.","slide":242,"shape":"6","bookPage":"140"},{"text":"4 Several celebrities, who are very concerned about their privacy, discussed the dangers of deepfake technology.","slide":243,"shape":"15","bookPage":"140"},{"text":"Positive arguments: The main advantage of; One good thing about; A real benefit of; The main argument in favour of.","slide":248,"shape":"14","bookPage":"141"},{"text":"Negative arguments: The main disadvantage of; The main worry about; One point against; One bad thing about; The main argument against; The problem with.","slide":248,"shape":"16","bookPage":"141"},{"text":"Positive arguments\nNegative arguments\nThe main advantage of; One good thing about; A real benefit of; The main argument in favour of\nThe main disadvantage of; The main worry about; One point against; One bad thing about; The main argument against; The problem with","slide":249,"shape":"12","bookPage":"141"},{"text":"1  The main advantage of robots is that they can do dangerous or boring jobs instead of humans.","slide":253,"shape":"6","bookPage":"141"},{"text":"2  The main worry about genetic engineering is that the new plant species may change human DNA.","slide":253,"shape":"7","bookPage":"141"},{"text":"3  A real benefit of medical imaging is that you can see clearly inside patients’ bodies.","slide":253,"shape":"8","bookPage":"141"},{"text":"4  The main disadvantage of robots is that they take jobs away from people.","slide":253,"shape":"9","bookPage":"141"},{"text":"Advantage 1: A real benefit of tablet computers is that they are portable.","slide":259,"shape":"15","bookPage":"141"},{"text":"Advantage 2: One good thing about tablet computers is that they offer many applications.","slide":259,"shape":"17","bookPage":"141"},{"text":"Disadvantage 1: The main disadvantage of tablet computers is that some models are expensive.","slide":259,"shape":"6","bookPage":"141"},{"text":"Disadvantage 2: One point against tablet computers is that small screens can make some tasks difficult.","slide":260,"shape":"16","bookPage":"141"},{"text":"1 What is the hook? Does it get your attention? If so, how? ‘To mimic people means to copy their speech, dress or behaviour.’ Yes. The familiar idea of copying people helps me understand copying nature.","slide":272,"shape":"16","bookPage":"142"},{"text":"2 What kind of background information does the paragraph include? The opening defines mimic and explains copying ideas from nature or natural processes.","slide":272,"shape":"18","bookPage":"142"},{"text":"3 According to the thesis statement, what is the topic and point of view? Topic: biomimicry. Point of view: it influences a huge range of everyday products.","slide":273,"shape":"16","bookPage":"142"},{"text":"3 (continued) How many paragraphs will the body of the article probably have, and what will each discuss? The article has four body paragraphs, each developing a product example: Velcro, adhesive, glasses and windows.","slide":273,"shape":"18","bookPage":"142"},{"text":"1 What is the hook? Does it get your attention? An actor’s head appears on a completely different actor’s body. Yes. This surprising image makes me want to understand how the technology works.","slide":296,"shape":"17","bookPage":"143"},{"text":"2 What kind of background information does the paragraph include? It defines deepfake, explains its connection to artificial intelligence and describes who can use it.","slide":296,"shape":"19","bookPage":"143"},{"text":"3 What is the topic and point of view? What will each paragraph probably discuss? Thesis: ‘This is causing both excitement and worry.’ Topic: deepfakes. Point of view: benefits and concerns. The body will discuss positive uses and problems.","slide":297,"shape":"17","bookPage":"143"},{"text":"4 Which introduction makes you more interested as a reader? Why? I find the deepfake introduction more interesting because the image is surprising.","slide":297,"shape":"19","bookPage":"143"},{"text":"A club app can help members follow changing plans. It is a tool that displays activities and meeting places. One advantage of the app is quick access to the schedule. However, members without a suitable device need another way to get the information.","slide":301,"shape":"6","bookPage":null},{"text":"Imagine losing small tools during a group project. A desk organizer is a tray that keeps those tools in separate sections. Its sections can be labelled for different items. I think it could help a group work more smoothly.","slide":302,"shape":"6","bookPage":null}];
